1
00:00:06,662 --> 00:00:14,092
TOEI COMPANY, LTD.

2
00:00:15,805 --> 00:00:23,805
CASTLE OF FLAMES

3
00:00:43,466 --> 00:00:45,366
CAST.

4
00:00:45,468 --> 00:00:48,369
OKAWA Hashizo as OMI Masato

5
00:00:48,471 --> 00:00:52,032
TAKAMINE Mieko as Tokiko
MITA Keiko as Yukino

6
00:00:52,108 --> 00:00:57,376
SUSUKIDA Kenji as ROKKAKU Naonoshin OKOCHI Denjiro
as OMI Morokage KUROKAWA Yataro as TAJIMI Shoji

7
00:00:57,480 --> 00:01:03,385
IZAVWA Ichiro as ROKKAKU Yugo BANDO Kichiva as SAGARA Tokei MIZUNO Hiroshi
as Rev. Gendo AKASHI Ushio as ONMI Katsumasa KAGAWA Ryosuke as Jinbei

8
00:01:22,805 --> 00:01:27,641
Directed by KATO Tai

9
00:01:34,850 --> 00:01:39,515
Some 400 years ago, on the
coast of the Inland Sea...

10
00:01:48,931 --> 00:01:51,491
The boat's in!

11
00:01:56,739 --> 00:01:58,400
Naonoshi

12
00:01:59,575 --> 00:02:06,447
A boat due in port two
months ago has not yet arrived.

13
00:02:07,283 --> 00:02:15,283
A sailboat from faraway
China could easily have...

14
00:02:17,827 --> 00:02:25,598
been swallowed up
by the sea in a storm.

15
00:02:29,572 --> 00:02:37,572
I dreamt last night that
the boat Masato was on

16
00:02:38,347 --> 00:02:40,145
sank in a storm.

17
00:02:43,152 --> 00:02:48,682
A lucky man I'd be if
only it would come true.

18
00:02:51,026 --> 00:02:52,585
Reporting, sir!
- What is it?

19
00:02:52,728 --> 00:02:55,373
The two men posted at
the port have returned

20
00:02:55,397 --> 00:02:58,276
to report the trading boat
has returned from China,

21
00:02:58,300 --> 00:03:00,860
with Yound Lord Masato
safely on board.

22
00:03:01,103 --> 00:03:02,537
What? He's returned?

23
00:03:03,873 --> 00:03:04,965
My lord!

24
00:03:07,743 --> 00:03:09,302
You say the young lord has returned?

25
00:03:09,445 --> 00:03:10,469
Yes, sir!

26
00:03:10,846 --> 00:03:15,511
The boat is safely in port with
Young Lord Masato on it?

27
00:03:15,618 --> 00:03:16,813
Yes, sir!

28
00:03:16,986 --> 00:03:19,318
Young Lord Masato has
seen the great big world.

29
00:03:20,055 --> 00:03:23,150
He's gained a wealth
of new knowledge.

30
00:03:23,659 --> 00:03:25,058
I'd love to hear his tales.

31
00:03:25,294 --> 00:03:28,940
Not only that, he'll
have great aspirations

32
00:03:28,964 --> 00:03:31,309
for government and industry,

33
00:03:31,333 --> 00:03:33,495
and we must help him realize them.

34
00:03:33,936 --> 00:03:35,404
In matters of ethics and religion, as well.

35
00:03:35,504 --> 00:03:36,403
Of course!

36
00:03:36,472 --> 00:03:38,236
There's hope for us.

37
00:03:38,707 --> 00:03:40,986
There's been a dark cloud
looming over Omi Castle

38
00:03:41,010 --> 00:03:42,910
ever since the passing of the old lord.

39
00:03:43,112 --> 00:03:47,606
Young Lord Masato will bring
a ray of light to the place.

40
00:03:51,520 --> 00:03:56,959
Are you so happy at
Masato's return, Yukino?

41
00:03:57,092 --> 00:03:58,116
Yes.

42
00:04:00,529 --> 00:04:05,262
How surprised Masato
will be to see the change...

43
00:04:05,968 --> 00:04:10,371
in the castle and in me.

44
00:04:11,774 --> 00:04:14,436
It's the lord.
Clear the way.

45
00:04:14,743 --> 00:04:16,006
Yukino?
- Yes.

46
00:04:26,188 --> 00:04:28,919
Some privacy, my lady.

47
00:04:29,491 --> 00:04:31,323
You may all go.

48
00:04:32,228 --> 00:04:33,354
You, too, Yukino.

49
00:04:33,495 --> 00:04:34,394
Yes, my lady.

50
00:04:39,134 --> 00:04:41,880
Your daughter seems to
be the only one happy

51
00:04:41,904 --> 00:04:43,929
at Masato's return.

52
00:04:44,106 --> 00:04:45,369
Indeed.

53
00:04:51,146 --> 00:04:57,176
How will you receive
Young Lord Masato, my lord?

54
00:04:58,921 --> 00:05:00,616
Well, now.

55
00:05:22,745 --> 00:05:27,492
Though far away, I fondly
recalled both my parents

56
00:05:27,516 --> 00:05:30,645
seeing me off as I sail.

57
00:05:33,322 --> 00:05:38,283
Now you tell me my father has passed...

58
00:05:39,261 --> 00:05:42,287
my uncle is lord, and my mother his wife?

59
00:05:43,332 --> 00:05:44,265
Yes.

60
00:05:47,636 --> 00:05:50,448
Where are my father's faithful vassals,

61
00:05:50,472 --> 00:05:52,270
Sagara lganosuke and Isshiki Shume?

62
00:05:52,474 --> 00:05:55,553
With the passing of the old lord,

63
00:05:55,577 --> 00:05:58,410
the two were dismissed and sent home.

64
00:05:58,714 --> 00:05:59,408
What?

65
00:05:59,481 --> 00:06:03,679
The elders took leave, presumably.

66
00:06:06,422 --> 00:06:11,870
My uncle, unlike my
father, is an ambitious man

67
00:06:11,894 --> 00:06:14,192
who would do anything for his ambitions.

68
00:06:15,964 --> 00:06:20,731
I cannot see my uncle like this.

69
00:06:22,538 --> 00:06:23,699
Nor my mother.

70
00:06:24,173 --> 00:06:26,073
I understand.

71
00:06:29,812 --> 00:06:31,280
Shoji...

72
00:06:31,714 --> 00:06:38,381
Did you come here secretly to fill me in?

73
00:06:38,654 --> 00:06:39,587
Yes.

74
00:06:40,622 --> 00:06:41,612
I thank you.

75
00:06:42,958 --> 00:06:44,824
What do you plan to
do, Young Lord Masato?

76
00:06:46,528 --> 00:06:48,018
Get to the truth.

77
00:06:48,964 --> 00:06:55,313
Prove that my father died, not of illness

78
00:06:55,337 --> 00:06:59,865
but by other cause, as you said yourself.

79
00:07:04,413 --> 00:07:07,007
You should return to the castle first.

80
00:07:07,149 --> 00:07:10,016
I've sent my crew back.

81
00:07:12,054 --> 00:07:16,218
I'll see Sagara lganosuke
and Isshiki Shume.

82
00:07:16,859 --> 00:07:18,122
They may be able to tell me something.

83
00:07:18,260 --> 00:07:18,726
Sir.

84
00:07:18,794 --> 00:07:22,025
ISSHIKI SHUME'S GRAVE

85
00:07:22,464 --> 00:07:26,230
Here lies my husband Shume.

86
00:07:29,605 --> 00:07:31,972
This is Isshiki Shume's grave?

87
00:07:32,141 --> 00:07:33,074
Yes.

88
00:07:37,012 --> 00:07:42,160
You say an envoy
came from the castle and

89
00:07:42,184 --> 00:07:45,586
ordered him to follow
his master in death?

90
00:07:45,788 --> 00:07:46,721
Yes.

91
00:07:47,589 --> 00:07:51,184
Shume probably knew something.

92
00:07:52,294 --> 00:07:57,275
It was, however, his
duty as samurai to follow

93
00:07:57,299 --> 00:08:00,564
his master in death.

94
00:08:01,904 --> 00:08:03,599
Do you truly believe that?

95
00:08:04,506 --> 00:08:09,854
My husband was always
concerned about you

96
00:08:09,878 --> 00:08:14,281
and wondered why you
went so far away.

97
00:08:14,750 --> 00:08:20,698
I went in search of
new knowledge that could

98
00:08:20,722 --> 00:08:25,319
help make this a land of
peace for all the people.

99
00:08:27,029 --> 00:08:31,843
But I couldn't be here for my father

100
00:08:31,867 --> 00:08:33,801
when he needed me most.

101
00:08:35,904 --> 00:08:39,306
I failed him as a son.

102
00:08:39,908 --> 00:08:46,991
I only ask humbly that
you tell my husband

103
00:08:47,015 --> 00:08:48,744
you're back safely.

104
00:08:51,687 --> 00:08:58,957
Shume, I remember
how you held me when...

105
00:08:59,695 --> 00:09:02,960
I was little and scolded me.

106
00:09:04,633 --> 00:09:08,934
I miss you, Old One...!

107
00:09:10,038 --> 00:09:11,301
Thank you...!

108
00:09:13,308 --> 00:09:14,707
Thank you...!

109
00:09:16,144 --> 00:09:17,578
You go back to the castle.

110
00:09:17,779 --> 00:09:19,508
And you?

111
00:09:20,215 --> 00:09:22,115
I'm going to Sagara Iganosuke's place.

112
00:09:23,385 --> 00:09:29,051
Shoji, you tell Yukino I'll be back soon.

113
00:09:29,424 --> 00:09:30,789
Yes, sir!
- Excuse me.

114
00:09:31,226 --> 00:09:34,457
Everybody, our gracious
lady sends you wine.

115
00:09:37,866 --> 00:09:41,613
We usually bring
back gold brocade, musk,

116
00:09:41,637 --> 00:09:43,537
silk, and satin damask from China.

117
00:09:43,639 --> 00:09:46,370
But we loaded the boat
with raw silk this time.

118
00:09:46,742 --> 00:09:48,938
Is raw silk worth that much?

119
00:09:54,716 --> 00:09:57,095
It's the universal currency in China,

120
00:09:57,119 --> 00:09:59,213
and worth a fortune.

121
00:10:02,190 --> 00:10:04,352
How about the women over there?

122
00:10:04,626 --> 00:10:06,822
Women back home are the best.

123
00:10:08,564 --> 00:10:10,328
There's your brother, Lady Yukino.

124
00:10:22,444 --> 00:10:24,674
I'm going to town on duty.

125
00:10:25,647 --> 00:10:26,910
No Young Lord Masato yet?

126
00:10:27,082 --> 00:10:30,347
No, only his crew.

127
00:10:30,619 --> 00:10:35,989
I want to see him and find
out if he feels the same.

128
00:10:36,892 --> 00:10:42,524
I know how you
missed him this past year.

129
00:10:43,298 --> 00:10:47,997
Brother, Young Lord Masato
would never change.

130
00:10:50,205 --> 00:10:51,673
I hope not.

131
00:10:52,040 --> 00:10:55,066
He came back right in time.

132
00:10:55,777 --> 00:10:57,655
Our Lord Morokage
and Toichi Masakiyo of

133
00:10:57,679 --> 00:11:01,274
Komano Castle are
arch rivals for this domain.

134
00:11:01,650 --> 00:11:04,642
One of them will win
and the other lose.

135
00:11:05,354 --> 00:11:09,834
Toichi Masakiyo is said
to have rounded up

136
00:11:09,858 --> 00:11:12,350
all the blind and drove
them into the sea.

137
00:11:13,261 --> 00:11:14,854
Why would he be so brutal?

138
00:11:14,963 --> 00:11:17,557
It's a Toichi ruse.

139
00:11:17,699 --> 00:11:18,791
A ruse?
- Yes.

140
00:11:19,267 --> 00:11:23,581
They're spreading rumors
that the blind are fleeing

141
00:11:23,605 --> 00:11:25,817
in fear to other lands,

142
00:11:25,841 --> 00:11:29,869
but they may actually
be here on a spy mission.

143
00:11:30,412 --> 00:11:31,880
Is that why you're going to town?

144
00:11:32,080 --> 00:11:35,311
Yes, to seize anyone
blind that's suspicious.

145
00:11:39,221 --> 00:11:43,419
Who killed Iganosuke?!

146
00:11:46,428 --> 00:11:51,628
I don't know who, or why!

147
00:11:53,535 --> 00:11:56,971
I reported it to the castle,
but to no avail.

148
00:12:00,008 --> 00:12:06,891
You say he was fishing
in the marsh in the back,

149
00:12:06,915 --> 00:12:09,577
when he was shot in
the chest by an arrow?!

150
00:12:10,852 --> 00:12:13,082
My father devoted his
life to service at the castle.

151
00:12:14,990 --> 00:12:17,118
So disgusted was I that
I became a peasant!

152
00:12:20,295 --> 00:12:21,956
I don't blame you.

153
00:12:24,232 --> 00:12:28,760
I came to ask Iganosuke something.

154
00:12:30,005 --> 00:12:32,872
We're having a meeting!

155
00:12:35,711 --> 00:12:37,372
Come on, we're having a meeting!

156
00:12:40,348 --> 00:12:42,646
Tokei! What's going on?

157
00:12:43,452 --> 00:12:44,749
I don't know yet.

158
00:12:46,921 --> 00:12:48,150
You come, too, Young Lord Masato.

159
00:12:48,523 --> 00:12:49,513
Me?
- Yes!

160
00:12:49,690 --> 00:12:51,249
Listen to what the villagers have to say.

161
00:12:51,425 --> 00:12:52,859
The village is in trouble.

162
00:12:53,027 --> 00:12:54,461
We were all awaiting your return.

163
00:12:54,662 --> 00:12:56,152
Young Lord Masato!

164
00:13:05,273 --> 00:13:06,900
It's Young Lord Masato!

165
00:13:07,008 --> 00:13:08,442
Young Lord Masato is back!

166
00:13:16,217 --> 00:13:18,117
Settle down, all of you!

167
00:13:23,391 --> 00:13:27,304
You're all aware that
Lord Morokage has decreed

168
00:13:27,328 --> 00:13:30,787
a reassessment of our farms and fields.

169
00:13:33,301 --> 00:13:36,737
That's because he's
going to increase taxes!

170
00:13:37,205 --> 00:13:40,140
Increase taxes for what?
War, that's what!

171
00:13:40,241 --> 00:13:42,719
We've had years of drought and want

172
00:13:42,743 --> 00:13:48,944
our taxes reduced, if not dropped.

173
00:13:49,350 --> 00:13:55,532
But we've been told we
have a new lord now,

174
00:13:55,556 --> 00:13:59,015
and a reassessment of
our farms and fields is due.

175
00:13:59,460 --> 00:14:02,452
What if they tell us to comply or else?

176
00:14:02,563 --> 00:14:03,860
We won't comply!

177
00:14:04,932 --> 00:14:06,593
No matter what?

178
00:14:06,734 --> 00:14:07,929
No matter what!

179
00:14:08,870 --> 00:14:12,067
Young Lord Masato!

180
00:14:18,613 --> 00:14:24,347
I promise to do what I can.

181
00:14:32,226 --> 00:14:33,751
Hey, Yugo!

182
00:14:34,829 --> 00:14:37,855
Shoji! Off duty today?

183
00:14:39,600 --> 00:14:41,090
What are you doing with the blind?

184
00:14:42,036 --> 00:14:43,299
They're spies from Komano Castle.

185
00:14:43,504 --> 00:14:47,873
No! We've lived in this town all our lives!

186
00:14:47,975 --> 00:14:48,965
Shut up!

187
00:14:49,877 --> 00:14:51,276
Take him away!

188
00:14:52,747 --> 00:15:00,747
I'm an outsider, but I've
done nothing wrong!

189
00:15:01,989 --> 00:15:04,822
Why must I be treated like this?

190
00:15:04,992 --> 00:15:07,393
Help me!

191
00:15:08,095 --> 00:15:09,062
Let's go!

192
00:15:09,730 --> 00:15:12,563
Help me!

193
00:15:13,134 --> 00:15:18,402
Make them confess!

194
00:15:25,646 --> 00:15:26,909
Confess, you stubborn spies!

195
00:15:37,425 --> 00:15:39,325
What are you waiting for?

196
00:15:39,727 --> 00:15:40,922
Off with their heads!

197
00:15:41,028 --> 00:15:42,291
But, sir...!

198
00:15:42,430 --> 00:15:44,956
Put their heads on display, as a warning!

199
00:15:45,199 --> 00:15:46,394
Understood?
- Yes, sir!

200
00:15:53,641 --> 00:15:57,475
Do you intend to let
Yukino see Masato?

201
00:15:58,646 --> 00:16:03,516
How she'll lament if I don't let her.

202
00:16:05,353 --> 00:16:07,549
You're a father, after all.

203
00:16:07,989 --> 00:16:14,137
Yukino lost her mother at a tender age,

204
00:16:14,161 --> 00:16:16,926
and I've always pitied her so.

205
00:16:17,098 --> 00:16:25,098
You do recall that
my ambition is to take

206
00:16:25,773 --> 00:16:33,773
this castle, then another, and another.

207
00:16:34,749 --> 00:16:35,910
You haven't forgotten.

208
00:16:36,317 --> 00:16:37,546
No, sir.

209
00:16:40,021 --> 00:16:42,888
I'm going to take Komano Castle.

210
00:16:43,090 --> 00:16:44,216
At last?

211
00:16:44,625 --> 00:16:50,257
And I'll send Masato
into the deadliest battles.

212
00:16:54,535 --> 00:16:58,281
If Yukino weds Masato,

213
00:16:58,305 --> 00:17:03,505
as my ambition grows,
so too will her worries.

214
00:17:03,677 --> 00:17:05,475
Keep that in mind.

215
00:17:30,004 --> 00:17:33,736
It's good to have you back, Masato.

216
00:17:35,242 --> 00:17:37,677
We were all awaiting your return.

217
00:17:38,546 --> 00:17:45,577
Let's set formalities aside and celebrate.

218
00:17:49,890 --> 00:17:55,454
Tell us all about
faraway lands, young lord.

219
00:17:59,100 --> 00:18:04,163
China is vast and it's sea is blue.

220
00:18:07,141 --> 00:18:13,706
Your heart is troubled
over your father's death.

221
00:18:14,748 --> 00:18:21,154
But think of me as
your father from now on.

222
00:18:27,394 --> 00:18:28,384
Masato!

223
00:18:33,734 --> 00:18:34,792
Masato?

224
00:19:18,345 --> 00:19:20,370
How did my father really die?

225
00:19:28,789 --> 00:19:29,950
Something is wrong.

226
00:19:40,167 --> 00:19:41,532
Was he murdered?

227
00:19:44,238 --> 00:19:45,672
If so, by whom?

228
00:19:52,746 --> 00:19:54,339
I must find proof.

229
00:20:04,391 --> 00:20:06,723
Find proof...

230
00:20:07,561 --> 00:20:08,824
Then get revenge!

231
00:20:10,965 --> 00:20:17,302
My father always wished for peace...

232
00:20:21,542 --> 00:20:29,542
While my uncle was
ambitious and bloodthirsty.

233
00:20:34,054 --> 00:20:41,085
How did my mother
come to share his bed?

234
00:20:51,005 --> 00:20:52,131
How?

235
00:20:52,773 --> 00:20:53,831
Masato?

236
00:20:57,878 --> 00:20:58,902
Masato?

237
00:21:08,222 --> 00:21:09,246
Masato?

238
00:21:25,239 --> 00:21:26,229
Masato?

239
00:22:01,742 --> 00:22:02,732
Masato!

240
00:22:06,714 --> 00:22:07,704
Masato!

241
00:22:10,984 --> 00:22:14,318
Masato, what's wrong with you?

242
00:22:16,090 --> 00:22:18,252
I've been waiting for you to return.

243
00:22:19,193 --> 00:22:21,252
I have much to tell you.

244
00:22:26,600 --> 00:22:29,297
It's Mother.
Don't you recognize me?

245
00:22:34,108 --> 00:22:35,303
It's Yukino.

246
00:22:35,709 --> 00:22:38,679
What's wrong, Young Lord Masato?

247
00:22:40,748 --> 00:22:43,342
What happened to you?

248
00:22:45,853 --> 00:22:47,378
What a sunny day.

249
00:22:47,855 --> 00:22:48,981
Masato!

250
00:22:49,723 --> 00:22:54,718
You're our only hope, our only pride.

251
00:22:56,130 --> 00:23:00,158
Please come to your senses.

252
00:23:03,404 --> 00:23:05,236
My fair Yukino...

253
00:23:06,273 --> 00:23:08,002
Are you a woman of virtue?

254
00:23:10,477 --> 00:23:13,742
A chaste woman?

255
00:23:13,947 --> 00:23:14,937
Young Lord Masato!

256
00:23:16,583 --> 00:23:23,285
Or a whore who sells
her beauty and chastity?

257
00:23:24,491 --> 00:23:25,549
Masato!

258
00:23:34,835 --> 00:23:35,961
She's scary!

259
00:23:37,905 --> 00:23:45,905
Like the angry sea that
swallows men right up!

260
00:24:00,160 --> 00:24:01,286
Young Lord Masato!

261
00:24:10,637 --> 00:24:16,719
Naonoshin, get two of
your most trusted men

262
00:24:16,743 --> 00:24:20,441
to keep an eye on Masato at all times.

263
00:24:20,781 --> 00:24:21,748
Yes, sir.

264
00:24:23,784 --> 00:24:27,220
Find out what caused his madness.

265
00:24:29,389 --> 00:24:31,824
The causes are many, I suspect.

266
00:24:33,727 --> 00:24:35,786
I'll see to it, sir

267
00:24:37,498 --> 00:24:39,592
You're here, Yugo.

268
00:24:43,070 --> 00:24:44,367
You summoned me?

269
00:24:45,305 --> 00:24:47,740
Naonoshin has told you everything.

270
00:24:48,175 --> 00:24:51,770
Depart today, and take
all the men you need.

271
00:24:53,213 --> 00:24:53,873
Yes, sir!

272
00:24:53,947 --> 00:25:00,296
When I decreed a reassessment
of all the farms and fields,

273
00:25:00,320 --> 00:25:05,815
those peasants had the gall to
demand that all debts be forgiven.

274
00:25:05,959 --> 00:25:07,324
Cancel all debts?

275
00:25:07,427 --> 00:25:11,174
The peasants claim to be impoverished and

276
00:25:11,198 --> 00:25:13,098
demand that all debts be cancel led.

277
00:25:13,333 --> 00:25:15,529
They consider taxes debts.

278
00:25:15,702 --> 00:25:18,171
Cancel taxes not yet paid?

279
00:25:18,539 --> 00:25:19,597
That's right.

280
00:25:21,041 --> 00:25:23,305
We can't go to war like that.

281
00:25:23,577 --> 00:25:24,567
Indeed.

282
00:25:26,847 --> 00:25:34,755
Seize and slay all peasants who defy me!

283
00:25:35,255 --> 00:25:39,817
What I want, I get by any means!

284
00:26:34,903 --> 00:26:37,929
Either I feign madness or be killed.

285
00:26:38,907 --> 00:26:39,874
Indeed.

286
00:26:40,275 --> 00:26:44,178
My uncle suspects, I'm sure.

287
00:26:44,446 --> 00:26:45,675
You must be on your guard.

288
00:26:45,981 --> 00:26:50,919
He has spies on me.

289
00:26:54,089 --> 00:26:55,113
Young Lord Masato!

290
00:26:57,960 --> 00:26:59,018
Young Lord Masato!

291
00:27:00,896 --> 00:27:02,421
How could you go
mad at a time like this?!

292
00:27:02,531 --> 00:27:04,761
He doesn't understand you, Yugo.

293
00:27:04,833 --> 00:27:06,028
It's deplorable!

294
00:27:12,741 --> 00:27:15,108
The Omi have a new lord...

295
00:27:16,278 --> 00:27:18,679
and are about to conquer the land.

296
00:27:19,515 --> 00:27:21,540
How could you come
back to us an invalid?

297
00:27:27,256 --> 00:27:31,557
What about my poor sister Yukino?

298
00:27:36,632 --> 00:27:38,122
What's so funny, you wimp?!

299
00:27:38,767 --> 00:27:41,634
Stop it, Yugo!

300
00:27:42,304 --> 00:27:45,831
He's gone mad because he's weak!

301
00:27:46,008 --> 00:27:47,032
He's a wimp!

302
00:27:47,709 --> 00:27:52,840
You know how long
I've waited for him, Shoji.

303
00:27:53,215 --> 00:27:55,650
For the sake of the castle.
For my sister's sake.

304
00:27:56,552 --> 00:28:02,047
When I see him like this,
it churns my innards!

305
00:28:03,625 --> 00:28:06,492
I can't help but call him a wimp!

306
00:28:07,496 --> 00:28:08,657
Do you blame me?

307
00:28:10,332 --> 00:28:12,164
Do you?

308
00:28:15,137 --> 00:28:18,732
But I won't cling on to lost hope.

309
00:28:19,408 --> 00:28:22,105
I'll tell myself Young Lord
Masato is dead, and go.

310
00:28:22,511 --> 00:28:23,569
Where to?

311
00:28:24,213 --> 00:28:25,942
There are signs of a peasant uprising.

312
00:28:26,582 --> 00:28:27,947
The lord commands me to quell it.

313
00:28:32,588 --> 00:28:33,646
Young Lord Masato!

314
00:28:48,637 --> 00:28:49,661
Young Lord Masato?

315
00:28:54,343 --> 00:28:59,509
He's a good man, an honest man.

316
00:28:59,715 --> 00:29:01,877
But he lacks thought.

317
00:29:01,984 --> 00:29:06,444
He acts without thinking.

318
00:29:07,990 --> 00:29:11,187
I've envied him for it.

319
00:29:14,296 --> 00:29:16,958
Yugo mentioned quelling a village uprising.

320
00:29:18,233 --> 00:29:19,860
Shoji...

321
00:29:22,004 --> 00:29:24,496
I made a promise to the villagers.

322
00:29:29,111 --> 00:29:31,705
You'll be departing shortly, Yugo.

323
00:29:34,516 --> 00:29:39,147
This is a farewell party.
Just the three of us.

324
00:29:44,826 --> 00:29:46,385
Father...

325
00:29:47,562 --> 00:29:49,087
I feel so sorry for Yukino.

326
00:29:53,902 --> 00:29:56,803
While I'm away...

327
00:29:57,506 --> 00:30:00,942
Will you find a good man for her?

328
00:30:01,343 --> 00:30:04,005
Don't say that, my brother.

329
00:30:04,212 --> 00:30:05,270
Why not?

330
00:30:05,447 --> 00:30:09,145
Young Lord Masato is the only man for me.

331
00:30:11,186 --> 00:30:14,884
But you've seen him, Yukino.

332
00:30:16,058 --> 00:30:22,259
Life is not as simple as you two think.

333
00:30:22,631 --> 00:30:28,434
It's full of compromises.

334
00:30:28,837 --> 00:30:29,861
Father!

335
00:30:31,139 --> 00:30:32,573
Brother...

336
00:30:32,874 --> 00:30:36,310
Do you really think Young
Lord Masato has gone mad?

337
00:30:36,478 --> 00:30:37,536
What?

338
00:30:37,879 --> 00:30:39,779
I don't be live it!

339
00:30:40,048 --> 00:30:41,106
What?

340
00:30:41,283 --> 00:30:46,619
Is there a reason for it, Father?

341
00:30:47,522 --> 00:30:48,751
What do you mean?

342
00:30:49,458 --> 00:30:57,024
A reason for Young Lord
Masato to feign madness.

343
00:30:57,099 --> 00:31:00,194
Don't be absurd!

344
00:31:00,302 --> 00:31:01,531
But...!

345
00:31:03,672 --> 00:31:04,730
Yukino.

346
00:31:05,574 --> 00:31:12,139
What makes you think
he's feigning madness?

347
00:31:15,584 --> 00:31:17,245
His eyes...
- What?

348
00:31:17,386 --> 00:31:23,587
Yes, when he looks at me and our lady.

349
00:31:24,793 --> 00:31:29,196
Those are not the eyes of a madman.

350
00:31:30,766 --> 00:31:34,930
You mean his eyes
have a life of their own?

351
00:31:35,704 --> 00:31:38,571
When he looks at you and our lady?

352
00:31:40,242 --> 00:31:42,472
Such are the eyes of a madman!

353
00:32:03,865 --> 00:32:05,094
Father...?

354
00:32:14,375 --> 00:32:15,495
Father!

355
00:32:35,555 --> 00:32:36,725
Your work?

356
00:32:38,795 --> 00:32:46,795
I'm done calculating the
taxes to be collected.

357
00:32:47,805 --> 00:32:49,325
You must be exhausted.

358
00:32:51,645 --> 00:32:52,905
No, I'm not.

359
00:33:34,315 --> 00:33:35,445
What's the matter?

360
00:33:36,215 --> 00:33:37,415
Someone's coming.

361
00:33:38,655 --> 00:33:42,595
Who would come to my bedchamber?

362
00:34:16,965 --> 00:34:19,015
The filth in there!

363
00:34:33,845 --> 00:34:40,185
There goes Yugo, off to
slaughter the peasants.

364
00:34:40,615 --> 00:34:45,685
Laying the groundwork
for my uncle's ambitions.

365
00:34:50,595 --> 00:34:53,155
I must keep my promise to the villagers.

366
00:34:56,465 --> 00:34:59,805
However, I have a job to do in the castle.

367
00:35:02,435 --> 00:35:05,505
Shoji, I saw my father last night.

368
00:35:05,745 --> 00:35:06,675
What?

369
00:35:06,815 --> 00:35:10,045
I wasn't dreaming.

370
00:35:12,345 --> 00:35:14,895
He was bloody and mortified,

371
00:35:14,915 --> 00:35:19,755
and trying to tell me something.

372
00:35:20,025 --> 00:35:21,285
And?

373
00:35:22,025 --> 00:35:26,695
He led me to my uncle
and mother's bedchamber.

374
00:35:26,835 --> 00:35:27,855
What?

375
00:35:28,495 --> 00:35:32,625
I know for certainty there's an awful secret.

376
00:35:33,975 --> 00:35:38,065
Shoji, I've made up my mind.

377
00:35:39,405 --> 00:35:43,175
I shall expose that secret!

378
00:35:44,215 --> 00:35:48,415
Soon, and no matter how.

379
00:35:57,595 --> 00:36:00,255
Is this so-called troupe here?

380
00:36:00,635 --> 00:36:02,225
Yes, in the main hall.

381
00:36:04,865 --> 00:36:09,495
Are you sure Masato
summoned them here?

382
00:36:10,345 --> 00:36:16,715
According to the spies I set on him, yes.

383
00:36:19,215 --> 00:36:27,215
And they're to perform
an act from the Kojiki?

384
00:36:30,895 --> 00:36:32,915
That should be interesting.

385
00:36:33,795 --> 00:36:35,235
Will you attend?

386
00:36:36,135 --> 00:36:44,135
It'll be a good chance for us to see if

387
00:36:45,505 --> 00:36:49,175
Masato is indeed mad, or not.

388
00:36:50,360 --> 00:36:51,620
Let's go.

389
00:38:09,670 --> 00:38:16,440
What evil lurks in the hearts of men.

390
00:38:17,140 --> 00:38:25,140
Young Lord Saohiko enticed
Young Lordss Saohime,

391
00:38:26,820 --> 00:38:34,820
wife of his older brother
the Divine Emperor,

392
00:38:38,130 --> 00:38:45,380
with a diabolical plot to rule the land,

393
00:38:45,400 --> 00:38:53,400
convincing her to take her husband's life.

394
00:40:09,190 --> 00:40:15,960
See my father standing
behind my mother, Yukino?

395
00:40:22,530 --> 00:40:30,530
Unaware of the evil plot,
the Divine Emperor

396
00:40:32,140 --> 00:40:40,140
laid his head on the
Empress' lap and slept.

397
00:40:41,190 --> 00:40:42,950
Enough prattle!

398
00:40:45,460 --> 00:40:47,450
Get on with the kill!

399
00:41:55,130 --> 00:41:57,060
That's enough!

400
00:41:57,400 --> 00:42:03,200
Did you see my uncle
and my mother, Shoji?

401
00:42:03,700 --> 00:42:06,400
I was right! I knew it!

402
00:42:10,810 --> 00:42:12,300
But...

403
00:42:14,210 --> 00:42:15,270
Young Lord Masato?

404
00:42:17,880 --> 00:42:24,160
Like Saohime, weeping
tears upon my father,

405
00:42:24,190 --> 00:42:26,250
my mother kept raising that sword to him.

406
00:42:26,420 --> 00:42:29,050
Only because the lord ordered her to.

407
00:42:29,330 --> 00:42:31,110
I hate my uncle for ordering her,

408
00:42:31,130 --> 00:42:32,820
and for killing my father.

409
00:42:33,970 --> 00:42:37,330
But my mother did comply.

410
00:42:39,570 --> 00:42:41,830
Must I get revenge on her?!

411
00:42:43,570 --> 00:42:46,240
I don't know what to tell you.

412
00:42:49,210 --> 00:42:53,880
How can I get revenge on my mother...

413
00:42:54,390 --> 00:42:56,250
with my own hands?

414
00:43:02,390 --> 00:43:05,730
Why did I summon that troupe?

415
00:43:08,730 --> 00:43:15,160
Why did I seek proof, and vow revenge?

416
00:43:17,480 --> 00:43:18,470
Young Lord Masato!

417
00:43:22,110 --> 00:43:25,640
Say something, Shoji!

418
00:43:27,920 --> 00:43:31,080
You are a thinking man...

419
00:43:31,520 --> 00:43:32,550
What?

420
00:43:32,820 --> 00:43:34,090
An agonizing man.

421
00:43:35,230 --> 00:43:39,220
But you're also a decisive
man who takes action.

422
00:43:39,860 --> 00:43:41,300
Take courage.

423
00:43:45,000 --> 00:43:46,630
Shoji...

424
00:43:47,840 --> 00:43:49,710
How I wish I could be like Yugo.

425
00:43:50,740 --> 00:43:54,230
Now more than ever.

426
00:44:02,650 --> 00:44:05,180
What is it, Yukino?

427
00:44:05,590 --> 00:44:12,830
Our lady wishes to see
Young Lord Masato in the parlor.

428
00:44:13,160 --> 00:44:15,600
So you came for him?

429
00:44:15,870 --> 00:44:16,800
Yes.

430
00:44:17,840 --> 00:44:20,630
I don't know if he'll understand.

431
00:44:22,410 --> 00:44:23,740
Did you hear her?

432
00:44:27,510 --> 00:44:30,740
Will you go to your mother's parlor?

433
00:44:33,450 --> 00:44:37,620
I wish my mother never bore me.

434
00:44:39,490 --> 00:44:40,860
Men are evil.

435
00:44:43,690 --> 00:44:45,030
All of them!

436
00:44:51,240 --> 00:44:53,000
You should never have been born, either.

437
00:44:53,170 --> 00:44:54,160
Young Lord Masato!

438
00:45:07,490 --> 00:45:09,610
Let's go to the temple.

439
00:45:11,790 --> 00:45:12,980
Come with me.

440
00:45:13,190 --> 00:45:17,390
Have you really gone
mad, Young Lord Masato?

441
00:45:24,970 --> 00:45:29,580
This is the gift you gave me,
along with your vow,

442
00:45:29,610 --> 00:45:31,370
just before you departed for China.

443
00:45:32,940 --> 00:45:34,570
Don't you remember?

444
00:45:35,810 --> 00:45:41,950
Upon this mirror, tell
me how you really feel.

445
00:45:43,050 --> 00:45:44,180
Oh, Young Lord Masato!

446
00:45:46,820 --> 00:45:49,850
You should marry a fool.

447
00:45:50,800 --> 00:45:54,320
There is none so fortunate as a fool.

448
00:45:57,030 --> 00:46:04,410
I had hoped you would
spare me of such words.

449
00:46:06,010 --> 00:46:12,030
Women paint their god
given faces with makeup

450
00:46:12,050 --> 00:46:14,640
and become something else.

451
00:46:16,990 --> 00:46:18,180
They're deceptive creatures.

452
00:46:18,620 --> 00:46:19,750
Sir Masato...!

453
00:46:20,830 --> 00:46:24,960
Please at least tell me the truth.

454
00:46:25,630 --> 00:46:27,960
What are you saying, Yukino?

455
00:46:29,900 --> 00:46:34,430
I just can't believe
Young Lord Masato is...

456
00:46:38,040 --> 00:46:42,480
Does that sound like
the laugh of a sane man?

457
00:46:45,450 --> 00:46:46,510
Get out!

458
00:46:47,450 --> 00:46:48,540
Young Lord Masato...!

459
00:46:49,220 --> 00:46:50,550
I hate women!

460
00:46:51,320 --> 00:46:53,920
Women are filthy!
Girls are filthy!

461
00:46:54,530 --> 00:46:55,790
Wives are filthy!

462
00:46:57,830 --> 00:46:58,990
Mothers are filthy!

463
00:47:01,170 --> 00:47:02,290
I hate women!

464
00:47:04,640 --> 00:47:06,300
I hate you...!

465
00:47:08,810 --> 00:47:09,830
Get out!

466
00:47:38,600 --> 00:47:45,630
Forgive me, Yukino...!

467
00:47:47,210 --> 00:47:50,700
Didn't you notice Masato's attitude?

468
00:47:53,080 --> 00:47:57,450
He suspects something and is trying to...

469
00:47:58,560 --> 00:48:00,850
ferret out what happened in his absence.

470
00:48:03,790 --> 00:48:10,670
He got that troupe to
perform the Saohime act!

471
00:48:13,900 --> 00:48:16,430
He isn't mad.

472
00:48:16,640 --> 00:48:18,920
He must be slain,

473
00:48:18,940 --> 00:48:20,840
like all the others who
would stand in my way!

474
00:48:28,220 --> 00:48:31,480
Were those peasants
taken captive by Yugo?

475
00:48:31,620 --> 00:48:36,790
Yes, 12 of them who
were plotting an uprising.

476
00:48:38,360 --> 00:48:40,060
Their disposition?

477
00:48:40,400 --> 00:48:44,310
Yugo sends word of a seaside execution

478
00:48:44,492 --> 00:48:45,922
as a warning to all others.

479
00:48:50,962 --> 00:48:53,332
Excuse me, my lord.

480
00:48:58,172 --> 00:48:59,632
Please!

481
00:49:00,402 --> 00:49:02,372
Please!

482
00:49:02,672 --> 00:49:05,162
Let me see the lord before you kill me!

483
00:49:05,342 --> 00:49:09,332
There's something I have to tell him!

484
00:49:19,992 --> 00:49:22,502
I am the son of Sagara Iganosuke,

485
00:49:22,522 --> 00:49:24,292
who long served at Omi Castle!

486
00:49:24,632 --> 00:49:28,492
Many of you owe him much!

487
00:49:29,032 --> 00:49:33,022
I am his son!
Ask Young Lord Masato!

488
00:49:43,282 --> 00:49:45,472
Young Lord Masato!

489
00:49:46,782 --> 00:49:49,652
Young Lord Masato...!

490
00:49:53,522 --> 00:49:55,782
Stop! Break it up!

491
00:50:08,742 --> 00:50:09,902
Tokei!

492
00:50:18,812 --> 00:50:20,582
Young Lord Masato's come to our rescue!

493
00:50:20,712 --> 00:50:22,942
It's Young Lord Masato!

494
00:50:24,392 --> 00:50:26,052
We're saved!

495
00:51:45,632 --> 00:51:49,162
He sleeps cradled in the
blessed light of the Buddha.

496
00:51:51,472 --> 00:51:58,642
Shall I send this nefarious
fiend to the nether world?

497
00:51:59,782 --> 00:52:01,372
Father...

498
00:52:02,822 --> 00:52:06,882
Shall that do you justice
and honor your life?

499
00:52:08,222 --> 00:52:09,752
Shall I...

500
00:52:14,232 --> 00:52:16,662
Shall I disgrace myself...

501
00:52:16,862 --> 00:52:22,562
with this cowardly act
of unholy vengeance...

502
00:52:23,042 --> 00:52:26,632
before the Buddha?

503
00:52:30,282 --> 00:52:32,342
Shall I?

504
00:53:04,612 --> 00:53:05,772
Why...?

505
00:53:15,692 --> 00:53:23,692
He has to suffer, much
more, as my father did...

506
00:53:24,972 --> 00:53:27,802
or it won't be revenge.

507
00:53:28,202 --> 00:53:29,262
Yes.

508
00:53:30,202 --> 00:53:31,532
Young Lord Masato...

509
00:53:31,672 --> 00:53:38,012
Our lady summons
you to her chamber.

510
00:53:40,612 --> 00:53:42,142
My mother...?

511
00:53:48,622 --> 00:53:56,622
At last the time has come.

512
00:53:59,632 --> 00:54:03,262
The lord killed Katsumasa.

513
00:54:05,142 --> 00:54:13,142
He and I and you know it.

514
00:54:18,492 --> 00:54:23,582
But there is one
thing you do not know.

515
00:54:23,922 --> 00:54:26,892
What might that be?

516
00:54:27,592 --> 00:54:32,542
When Katsumasa was taken ill,

517
00:54:32,572 --> 00:54:35,062
the lord raped me.

518
00:54:36,672 --> 00:54:44,672
I knew the lord
always cared for you...

519
00:54:45,112 --> 00:54:47,312
but rape you...?

520
00:54:47,912 --> 00:54:52,982
I lay awake at night,
tormented, Naonoshin.

521
00:54:54,392 --> 00:54:59,882
When the lord told me
to slay my husband...

522
00:55:00,462 --> 00:55:05,422
I thought of dying with him...

523
00:55:05,932 --> 00:55:08,632
if only to repent.

524
00:55:11,972 --> 00:55:14,272
How could I slay my own husband?

525
00:55:15,642 --> 00:55:20,192
But he was to be slain by the lord,

526
00:55:20,212 --> 00:55:22,912
and I, sadly, was to live.

527
00:55:24,322 --> 00:55:28,252
The lord then became
master of Omi Castle...

528
00:55:28,962 --> 00:55:34,052
and I, his wife, upon your advice.

529
00:55:36,632 --> 00:55:40,342
I thought it best for
the castle and that

530
00:55:40,372 --> 00:55:45,932
the strong shall rule in
these troubled times.

531
00:55:47,672 --> 00:55:49,902
I am but a woman...

532
00:55:50,312 --> 00:55:58,312
A weak woman unable
to defy the lord...

533
00:56:05,232 --> 00:56:07,322
unable to die.

534
00:56:08,062 --> 00:56:14,472
I could only await Masato's return...

535
00:56:15,102 --> 00:56:19,822
to throw myself at his feet for forgiveness

536
00:56:19,842 --> 00:56:23,402
and accept my fate, come what may.

537
00:56:23,742 --> 00:56:28,682
But Masato has returned a madman...

538
00:56:29,282 --> 00:56:33,692
and I find myself in despair once more.

539
00:56:37,162 --> 00:56:41,602
That I am willing to sacrifice myself for

540
00:56:41,632 --> 00:56:45,332
the peace of the
castle is but a noble lie.

541
00:56:46,102 --> 00:56:51,772
I wish to confess all to Masato.

542
00:56:52,142 --> 00:56:53,232
But...

543
00:56:53,342 --> 00:56:59,522
Though he is mad and
unable to understand,

544
00:56:59,552 --> 00:57:03,572
if I could tell the secret I keep...

545
00:57:04,082 --> 00:57:08,682
how it would clear my soul.

546
00:57:08,862 --> 00:57:11,722
But you mustn't.
- Why not?

547
00:57:11,892 --> 00:57:19,462
There are rumors he
is feigning madness.

548
00:57:25,012 --> 00:57:33,012
Then all the more I place
my fate in his hands.

549
00:57:34,182 --> 00:57:38,162
Should Young Lord Masato
learn of what the lord

550
00:57:38,192 --> 00:57:44,182
has done, the castle will
be thrown into turmoil.

551
00:57:44,322 --> 00:57:50,202
I betrayed my own child.

552
00:57:50,962 --> 00:57:55,332
You're a parent.
Surely you know my pain.

553
00:57:55,502 --> 00:57:59,232
I do, which makes it
all the more difficult.

554
00:57:59,442 --> 00:58:01,702
I hear Masato's footsteps.

555
00:58:02,282 --> 00:58:05,912
Leave me alone with him.

556
00:58:06,112 --> 00:58:09,082
I'll hide behind the screen.

557
00:58:09,182 --> 00:58:10,342
No!

558
00:58:10,552 --> 00:58:12,702
If he proves to be sane,

559
00:58:12,722 --> 00:58:14,692
I'll come right out and deal with him.

560
00:58:14,822 --> 00:58:15,722
Are you sure?

561
00:58:15,792 --> 00:58:21,962
I've picked up a few
tricks in my old age.

562
00:58:41,012 --> 00:58:45,422
Masato, do you understand me?

563
00:58:49,822 --> 00:58:52,092
Even if you don't,
please hear me out.

564
00:58:53,032 --> 00:58:56,162
I did not kill your father.

565
00:58:57,102 --> 00:59:00,862
Please believe me, Masato!

566
00:59:02,872 --> 00:59:03,892
Please!

567
00:59:04,042 --> 00:59:05,132
You beast!

568
00:59:05,972 --> 00:59:06,962
Masato!

569
00:59:07,272 --> 00:59:08,472
Look at this!

570
00:59:10,682 --> 00:59:12,482
The bed of the beast!

571
00:59:14,212 --> 00:59:15,342
What filth!

572
00:59:17,922 --> 00:59:21,682
Your aging bodies writhing in grease...

573
00:59:22,792 --> 00:59:27,822
burning with unholy lust, like animals!

574
00:59:28,132 --> 00:59:29,192
Masato!

575
00:59:29,802 --> 00:59:31,062
Shame on you!

576
00:59:35,542 --> 00:59:40,472
Not that you beasts have any shame.

577
00:59:46,212 --> 00:59:48,652
The stench!

578
00:59:49,182 --> 00:59:51,312
The stench of it all!

579
00:59:51,452 --> 00:59:52,542
Yes.

580
00:59:54,192 --> 01:00:00,322
I'd forgotten what it
meant to be a mother.

581
01:00:01,092 --> 01:00:02,192
Enough!

582
01:00:03,962 --> 01:00:07,982
This animal isn't a
tenth of the man your

583
01:00:08,002 --> 01:00:11,402
former husband was.

584
01:00:13,012 --> 01:00:15,102
He's a thief!
A murderer!

585
01:00:16,842 --> 01:00:23,752
Your words pierce
my heart like a sword!

586
01:00:24,282 --> 01:00:27,412
Why do you share that beast's bed?

587
01:00:27,492 --> 01:00:32,652
But don't stop.
I make no excuses.

588
01:00:32,962 --> 01:00:37,522
Hurl all your hateful words at me!

589
01:00:38,532 --> 01:00:43,802
I want to...

590
01:00:44,402 --> 01:00:48,862
But I keep hearing Father's voice.

591
01:00:50,642 --> 01:00:53,272
Weak is a woman.

592
01:00:54,452 --> 01:00:59,482
Spare your mother from
further torment, he says.

593
01:01:01,862 --> 01:01:04,422
I keep hearing his voice.

594
01:01:06,992 --> 01:01:08,222
Masato!

595
01:01:09,202 --> 01:01:15,972
You haven't gone mad, have you?!

596
01:01:17,372 --> 01:01:18,532
Masato!

597
01:01:19,242 --> 01:01:20,542
You beast!

598
01:01:23,142 --> 01:01:24,802
I saw that screen move.

599
01:01:26,712 --> 01:01:29,342
So that's where he is...

600
01:01:29,822 --> 01:01:31,252
That lustful beast!

601
01:01:32,452 --> 01:01:33,582
Masato!

602
01:01:42,632 --> 01:01:44,322
Naonoshi

603
01:01:47,702 --> 01:01:49,532
Masato!

604
01:01:52,272 --> 01:01:53,362
Masato!

605
01:02:13,711 --> 01:02:16,841
He's a madman!
Leave him alone!

606
01:02:29,001 --> 01:02:32,231
Stay back!
- Father!

607
01:02:42,311 --> 01:02:45,641
After him!

608
01:02:46,711 --> 01:02:47,871
What?

609
01:02:48,151 --> 01:02:50,741
Masato has slain Naonoshin?

610
01:02:50,851 --> 01:02:51,651
Yes, sir!

611
01:02:51,751 --> 01:02:53,341
Well, seize him!

612
01:02:53,691 --> 01:02:54,521
Yes, sir!

613
01:02:54,691 --> 01:02:57,591
By any means!

614
01:02:58,091 --> 01:02:58,961
Now!

615
01:02:59,031 --> 01:03:01,521
There he is!

616
01:03:04,261 --> 01:03:06,961
Leave them to me and go!

617
01:03:07,371 --> 01:03:09,101
Young Lord Masato!

618
01:03:13,271 --> 01:03:15,741
Please!

619
01:03:17,211 --> 01:03:18,271
Young Lord Masato!

620
01:03:22,921 --> 01:03:26,221
Shoji, you dare defy our lord?!

621
01:03:55,081 --> 01:03:56,851
Young Lord Masato...!

622
01:04:20,171 --> 01:04:24,111
How could I kill Yukino's father?!

623
01:04:24,711 --> 01:04:28,151
Of all men...!

624
01:05:08,691 --> 01:05:09,781
Hey!

625
01:05:13,661 --> 01:05:14,961
Eat some food.

626
01:05:34,281 --> 01:05:35,511
Thanks.

627
01:05:39,791 --> 01:05:41,981
This is yours.

628
01:05:47,191 --> 01:05:52,961
Where were you going
in that puny boat?

629
01:05:54,301 --> 01:05:56,431
Nowhere.

630
01:05:56,801 --> 01:06:02,241
We thought you
were rowing toward us.

631
01:06:02,541 --> 01:06:06,781
That was just the
wind and the waves.

632
01:06:07,381 --> 01:06:09,541
I see.

633
01:06:20,361 --> 01:06:25,421
The boat we were
after got away from us...

634
01:06:25,701 --> 01:06:32,001
and you were our only catch.

635
01:06:35,111 --> 01:06:36,671
Are you pirates?

636
01:06:36,811 --> 01:06:38,071
That's right.

637
01:06:38,741 --> 01:06:41,011
Now eat your food.

638
01:06:51,021 --> 01:06:52,961
Is it good?

639
01:06:54,361 --> 01:06:56,951
No, not really.

640
01:06:58,401 --> 01:07:00,301
An honest guy!

641
01:07:03,701 --> 01:07:06,301
Where's your turf?

642
01:07:06,771 --> 01:07:09,211
Korea, China, anywhere.

643
01:07:11,141 --> 01:07:12,671
I see.

644
01:07:14,951 --> 01:07:16,751
You're the Japanese
pirates I heard about.

645
01:07:16,851 --> 01:07:21,081
It's every man for
himself in this world!

646
01:07:24,721 --> 01:07:27,961
How about it?
Want to join us?

647
01:07:29,331 --> 01:07:31,351
Well...

648
01:07:36,241 --> 01:07:39,141
I've nowhere else to go.

649
01:07:39,341 --> 01:07:41,271
Meet the captain.

650
01:07:46,351 --> 01:07:50,301
Japan is too small for all of us.

651
01:07:51,051 --> 01:07:52,281
Right?

652
01:07:53,051 --> 01:07:58,181
How did you become a pirate?

653
01:07:59,491 --> 01:08:00,621
How?

654
01:08:07,631 --> 01:08:13,301
I was the son of a
peasant subject of the Omi.

655
01:08:14,611 --> 01:08:16,411
The Omi?
- Yes.

656
01:08:17,741 --> 01:08:25,311
My old man couldn't pay his
taxes and hanged himself.

657
01:08:27,751 --> 01:08:33,351
I ran off from the village
but had nowhere to go.

658
01:08:33,961 --> 01:08:38,921
You must hate the Omi then.

659
01:08:39,401 --> 01:08:40,891
Of course!

660
01:08:41,801 --> 01:08:46,801
I wish I could get these
men to attack the castle.

661
01:08:47,341 --> 01:08:48,541
In revenge?

662
01:08:48,871 --> 01:08:50,171
Sure!

663
01:08:50,941 --> 01:08:55,971
Make them suffer the
way peasants have.

664
01:08:58,751 --> 01:09:04,491
Many others must
feel the same way.

665
01:09:05,421 --> 01:09:06,951
They all do!

666
01:09:07,991 --> 01:09:10,991
All of the peasant subjects of the Omi!

667
01:09:12,901 --> 01:09:18,751
Some prince promised
to help the peasants,

668
01:09:18,771 --> 01:09:20,741
but I don't trust him!

669
01:09:23,641 --> 01:09:26,561
He's all talk,

670
01:09:26,581 --> 01:09:31,071
and no better than the others!

671
01:09:32,181 --> 01:09:35,851
Not that I've ever seen him.

672
01:09:38,491 --> 01:09:41,121
A storm is coming!

673
01:09:41,391 --> 01:09:42,951
It's going to be a stormy night.

674
01:09:58,081 --> 01:10:00,601
The people are all looking for relief.

675
01:10:01,681 --> 01:10:05,171
I can't just sit here.

676
01:10:08,891 --> 01:10:13,521
In despair, they'll seek
revenge on the Omi.

677
01:10:15,661 --> 01:10:19,661
Just as I shall seek
revenge for my father...

678
01:10:20,101 --> 01:10:22,761
on that tyrant in Omi Castle.

679
01:10:26,741 --> 01:10:29,281
The revenge of the
Omi subjects and the

680
01:10:29,311 --> 01:10:34,681
the revenge of the heir of
their peace loving lord.

681
01:10:34,811 --> 01:10:38,811
They are but one.

682
01:10:39,021 --> 01:10:42,111
One in me, Masato!

683
01:10:46,991 --> 01:10:51,431
I can't join these pirates.

684
01:10:52,261 --> 01:10:54,101
I must return to the castle.

685
01:10:55,001 --> 01:10:58,661
But what about Yukino?

686
01:11:02,041 --> 01:11:03,911
I can't...!

687
01:11:06,181 --> 01:11:10,481
I can never hold
Yukino in my arms again!

688
01:11:45,451 --> 01:11:47,111
Father!

689
01:11:52,421 --> 01:11:53,951
Father...?

690
01:11:54,661 --> 01:11:56,651
Are you telling me to
return to the castle?

691
01:11:57,601 --> 01:12:00,661
To rise up?

692
01:12:07,041 --> 01:12:08,401
Father!

693
01:12:10,241 --> 01:12:12,511
Father!

694
01:12:22,451 --> 01:12:30,451
You refuse to come to my bed?

695
01:12:33,001 --> 01:12:34,631
Tokiko...

696
01:12:36,971 --> 01:12:38,531
My lord...

697
01:12:45,081 --> 01:12:48,161
Masato reviled me,

698
01:12:48,181 --> 01:12:53,381
and I watched him
stab Naonoshin to death.

699
01:12:56,321 --> 01:13:03,131
I can only wonder where
he is, what he's doing.

700
01:13:03,801 --> 01:13:05,531
Masato won't come back.

701
01:13:05,661 --> 01:13:06,931
Why not?

702
01:13:07,371 --> 01:13:09,271
His madman act is exposed.

703
01:13:10,471 --> 01:13:12,841
He will not live.
- My lord!

704
01:13:13,411 --> 01:13:17,901
You'd rather be Masato's
mother than my wife?!

705
01:13:18,811 --> 01:13:20,181
Yes.

706
01:13:20,811 --> 01:13:24,511
You know exactly how I feel.

707
01:13:24,881 --> 01:13:26,281
Why, you!

708
01:13:26,951 --> 01:13:28,481
Come to my chamber, woman!

709
01:13:28,591 --> 01:13:30,151
My lord!
- Come now!

710
01:13:34,261 --> 01:13:35,891
My lord...

711
01:13:36,231 --> 01:13:41,721
You can no longer bully me.

712
01:13:42,031 --> 01:13:43,201
All right!

713
01:13:43,971 --> 01:13:45,901
You've made yourself clear.

714
01:13:46,711 --> 01:13:51,581
But listen to me!

715
01:13:53,551 --> 01:13:55,991
I have ambitions, yes,

716
01:13:56,021 --> 01:14:00,951
of taking this castle
and ruling the land.

717
01:14:01,651 --> 01:14:05,031
And I want you for my wife,

718
01:14:05,119 --> 01:14:06,879
to have and to hold!

719
01:14:07,449 --> 01:14:08,609
Tokiko!

720
01:14:08,889 --> 01:14:10,359
My lord...!
- Reporting!

721
01:14:11,489 --> 01:14:12,649
What is it?

722
01:14:14,989 --> 01:14:17,829
Sir Rokkaku Yugo has just returned.

723
01:14:29,169 --> 01:14:31,769
Yugo, good job.

724
01:14:32,179 --> 01:14:33,539
What do you report?

725
01:14:35,409 --> 01:14:36,709
It's out of control.

726
01:14:36,819 --> 01:14:37,869
What?

727
01:14:38,719 --> 01:14:44,049
Quell one uprising
and there's another.

728
01:14:44,419 --> 01:14:48,189
We'd go from village to
village putting out fires.

729
01:14:48,329 --> 01:14:49,619
Bastards!

730
01:14:52,659 --> 01:14:56,229
That did it!

731
01:14:57,339 --> 01:15:00,169
We're going to war!

732
01:15:02,209 --> 01:15:08,979
We'll subdue those rebels
and surge on Komano Castle!

733
01:15:09,949 --> 01:15:10,969
My lord!

734
01:15:11,649 --> 01:15:12,449
What?

735
01:15:12,519 --> 01:15:14,819
What became of my
father in my absence?

736
01:15:14,949 --> 01:15:16,179
Masato killed him.

737
01:15:16,289 --> 01:15:19,159
And my sister Yukino?

738
01:15:19,389 --> 01:15:21,189
He drove her to despair.

739
01:15:28,069 --> 01:15:29,229
That wretch!

740
01:15:30,269 --> 01:15:34,209
So he was feigning madness!

741
01:15:41,749 --> 01:15:44,219
Yugo, you're back.

742
01:15:46,489 --> 01:15:48,009
Are you here to visit
your father's grave?

743
01:15:48,089 --> 01:15:49,109
Yes.

744
01:15:49,589 --> 01:15:52,349
But no sutras, reverend.

745
01:15:53,859 --> 01:15:54,989
Why not?

746
01:15:55,529 --> 01:15:57,999
Consider it a blessing.

747
01:15:58,159 --> 01:15:59,529
A blessing?

748
01:16:00,869 --> 01:16:04,959
It's more like a lullaby to me.

749
01:16:05,439 --> 01:16:06,839
A lullaby?

750
01:16:07,739 --> 01:16:13,079
Has something been awakened in you?

751
01:16:13,209 --> 01:16:16,439
Yes, something that burns inside me...

752
01:16:16,849 --> 01:16:19,909
and the only thing I shall live for.

753
01:16:21,419 --> 01:16:23,079
And what is this thing?

754
01:16:23,859 --> 01:16:26,119
Something you would stop me from.

755
01:16:28,059 --> 01:16:29,549
Revenge!

756
01:16:58,219 --> 01:16:59,689
Yukino...

757
01:17:00,129 --> 01:17:02,319
What have you been
doing since his death?

758
01:17:03,359 --> 01:17:09,629
Coming here to
offer flowers every day.

759
01:17:09,969 --> 01:17:11,459
I see...

760
01:17:15,139 --> 01:17:16,539
Yukino...

761
01:17:17,339 --> 01:17:19,869
I promise to find Masato and Kill him!

762
01:17:21,009 --> 01:17:22,109
What?

763
01:17:22,849 --> 01:17:25,179
I swear I will!

764
01:17:25,249 --> 01:17:26,219
No!

765
01:17:26,349 --> 01:17:27,749
What do you mean no?

766
01:17:27,949 --> 01:17:29,979
He's our enemy!

767
01:17:30,289 --> 01:17:31,849
He killed our father and destroyed you!

768
01:17:31,919 --> 01:17:33,919
No!
- Yukino!

769
01:17:34,129 --> 01:17:36,689
I love Young Lord Masato.

770
01:17:36,829 --> 01:17:39,659
I always will, no matter what!

771
01:17:39,829 --> 01:17:40,919
What?

772
01:17:41,229 --> 01:17:43,169
Yukino!
- Hey, Yugo!

773
01:17:46,539 --> 01:17:48,839
Someone saw Young Lord Masato in town.

774
01:17:48,939 --> 01:17:50,809
What? You wait here!

775
01:18:02,989 --> 01:18:04,319
Why, you!

776
01:18:04,659 --> 01:18:05,889
What the...?!

777
01:18:06,059 --> 01:18:07,249
Sorry!

778
01:18:30,079 --> 01:18:31,449
Young Lord Masato!

779
01:18:33,049 --> 01:18:36,319
Oh, Young Lord Masato!
You came back!

780
01:18:39,289 --> 01:18:43,059
I stabbed Naonoshin
to death by mistake.

781
01:18:44,929 --> 01:18:46,299
Will you forgive me?

782
01:18:46,569 --> 01:18:52,729
Young Lord Masato, take me with
you and flee somewhere far away.

783
01:18:54,469 --> 01:18:58,409
I wish I could...!

784
01:18:59,309 --> 01:19:06,479
I shall forget that my
father was slain by you.

785
01:19:07,419 --> 01:19:11,079
My brother is after you to get revenge.

786
01:19:11,359 --> 01:19:15,879
But I shall forsake my
brother, to be with you.

787
01:19:16,659 --> 01:19:17,819
Yukino!

788
01:19:19,199 --> 01:19:26,999
I can never forget
all the caring words...

789
01:19:27,469 --> 01:19:29,839
you have spoken to me.

790
01:19:30,339 --> 01:19:32,369
Yukino...

791
01:19:32,879 --> 01:19:35,779
My feelings for you are unchanged.

792
01:19:37,649 --> 01:19:39,479
But...

793
01:19:40,919 --> 01:19:42,249
Forgive me!

794
01:19:47,229 --> 01:19:50,459
Then, Young Lord Masato...

795
01:19:51,129 --> 01:19:58,199
Did you not come back for me?

796
01:19:59,369 --> 01:20:05,109
I'm afraid not.

797
01:20:08,549 --> 01:20:13,419
There's something I
have to do for my father.

798
01:20:13,549 --> 01:20:18,249
Am I a hindrance to you?

799
01:20:20,789 --> 01:20:22,759
Must I say?

800
01:20:29,599 --> 01:20:30,969
Forgive me...!

801
01:20:48,449 --> 01:20:51,389
It's live or die!

802
01:20:51,789 --> 01:20:54,159
All 120 villages have risen up!

803
01:20:55,159 --> 01:20:57,239
The castle soldiers will
come out in full force!

804
01:20:57,259 --> 01:20:58,589
United we stand!

805
01:21:00,029 --> 01:21:01,799
We've had it!

806
01:21:01,899 --> 01:21:04,059
Lord Morokage is not our sovereign!

807
01:21:04,169 --> 01:21:06,399
Young Lord Masato is!

808
01:21:10,579 --> 01:21:15,139
Round up all the villagers everywhere!

809
01:21:15,549 --> 01:21:18,809
Victory will be ours!

810
01:22:26,149 --> 01:22:27,919
No, Young Lord Masato!

811
01:22:32,059 --> 01:22:33,889
Tell my uncle I'm back!

812
01:22:34,029 --> 01:22:37,759
My lord!

813
01:22:38,659 --> 01:22:42,429
Will you avenge your father?

814
01:22:42,599 --> 01:22:43,499
Yes!

815
01:22:43,569 --> 01:22:45,369
Masato is a master swordsman.

816
01:22:45,669 --> 01:22:47,039
I realize that.

817
01:22:54,779 --> 01:22:55,839
Fine!

818
01:22:57,079 --> 01:23:02,179
You two shall duel
before the entire castle.

819
01:23:02,319 --> 01:23:03,149
Yes, sir!

820
01:23:03,219 --> 01:23:05,499
Before their duel,

821
01:23:05,519 --> 01:23:10,119
Masato and Yugo shall drink this wine.

822
01:23:11,499 --> 01:23:19,499
The one laced with
this poison is for Masato.

823
01:23:25,339 --> 01:23:28,509
This one is for Yugo.
Do not mistake them.

824
01:23:36,889 --> 01:23:38,909
The white sheathed one is for Masato.

825
01:23:39,689 --> 01:23:41,849
The blue sheathed one is for Yugo.

826
01:23:42,859 --> 01:23:44,059
Understood?

827
01:23:48,299 --> 01:23:55,669
Yugo's sword shall
have a poisoned tip.

828
01:23:56,739 --> 01:24:02,199
Struck by this sword,
Masato shall not survive.

829
01:24:03,179 --> 01:24:05,149
Do not mistake them.

830
01:24:10,559 --> 01:24:13,149
What's going on?

831
01:24:13,889 --> 01:24:16,089
No, Young Lord Masato!

832
01:24:17,959 --> 01:24:19,399
Uncle!
- Young Lord Masato!

833
01:24:19,499 --> 01:24:21,989
Vow to all that you will stop...

834
01:24:22,499 --> 01:24:28,669
oppressing the people and making war!

835
01:24:28,869 --> 01:24:32,399
Stop babbling and know your place!

836
01:24:32,579 --> 01:24:37,069
Repent, right now,
for murdering my father!

837
01:24:37,349 --> 01:24:41,219
You have truly gone mad!

838
01:24:43,419 --> 01:24:44,509
Masato!

839
01:24:45,989 --> 01:24:50,689
Are you ready to avenge your father?

840
01:24:51,159 --> 01:24:52,289
I challenge you!

841
01:24:54,999 --> 01:24:57,259
I don't want to fight you.
- You coward!

842
01:24:57,799 --> 01:25:00,929
Draw your sword!

843
01:25:01,509 --> 01:25:02,669
Wait.

844
01:25:04,079 --> 01:25:05,909
Masato...

845
01:25:06,679 --> 01:25:09,889
As your uncle, I shall
permit you to fight,

846
01:25:09,909 --> 01:25:13,939
fair and square, in a proper duel.

847
01:25:33,739 --> 01:25:35,139
You give me no choice.

848
01:25:43,749 --> 01:25:48,689
First, a drink of wine to calm the spirit.

849
01:26:09,400 --> 01:26:12,140
Masato, let me take that drink!

850
01:26:12,240 --> 01:26:13,260
No!

851
01:26:13,510 --> 01:26:15,170
Stay out of this, woman!

852
01:26:15,380 --> 01:26:17,970
This may be the last I see of my son!

853
01:26:18,710 --> 01:26:23,380
Let me have a final drink with him!

854
01:26:23,450 --> 01:26:25,220
No, I said!

855
01:26:27,660 --> 01:26:31,490
Yugo, what are you waiting for?
Take him!

856
01:27:29,720 --> 01:27:30,880
Masato!

857
01:28:34,980 --> 01:28:36,780
Masato! Watch out!

858
01:28:41,390 --> 01:28:42,480
Mother!

859
01:28:42,590 --> 01:28:44,180
Slay him!

860
01:28:44,830 --> 01:28:46,320
Slay Masato!

861
01:29:03,240 --> 01:29:07,880
No bloodshed shall wash away my sin!

862
01:29:08,450 --> 01:29:10,440
Forget me and flee!

863
01:29:11,990 --> 01:29:13,220
Mother!

864
01:29:19,030 --> 01:29:20,500
Stand back!

865
01:29:25,400 --> 01:29:26,830
Wait, Morokage!

866
01:29:33,840 --> 01:29:37,800
Morokage, you coward...!

867
01:29:55,860 --> 01:29:57,020
Leave him!

868
01:30:21,820 --> 01:30:23,090
Close the gate!

869
01:30:49,520 --> 01:30:51,750
They're coming!

870
01:30:51,920 --> 01:30:54,150
It's a rebel army!

871
01:31:29,120 --> 01:31:30,820
Get the firing squad!

872
01:31:36,130 --> 01:31:37,620
Torch the castle!

873
01:31:38,670 --> 01:31:40,630
Throw the torches!

874
01:31:57,390 --> 01:31:59,950
My lord!

875
01:32:01,360 --> 01:32:04,330
My lord!

876
01:32:37,160 --> 01:32:38,820
Fire!

877
01:32:38,960 --> 01:32:40,360
Go!

878
01:33:25,170 --> 01:33:27,500
Break it down!

879
01:34:02,640 --> 01:34:03,870
Damn you!

880
01:35:38,870 --> 01:35:40,310
Young Lord Masato!

881
01:35:44,580 --> 01:35:46,210
Young Lord Masato!

882
01:35:47,110 --> 01:35:48,280
You women, flee!

883
01:38:04,320 --> 01:38:06,010
Yukino...

884
01:38:07,120 --> 01:38:11,490
I wanted to spare you of all this.

885
01:38:14,060 --> 01:38:15,720
Forgive me...!

886
01:38:24,310 --> 01:38:28,830
I had no other recourse.

887
01:38:30,410 --> 01:38:32,140
Yukino...

888
01:38:32,610 --> 01:38:37,410
Cherishing your pure and innocent love...

889
01:38:37,990 --> 01:38:42,950
I dedicated my life to
the good of the people.

890
01:38:44,630 --> 01:38:46,250
Forgive me...

891
01:38:48,800 --> 01:38:50,700
Forgive me...!

892
01:39:02,080 --> 01:39:04,550
THE END

893
01:39:04,680 --> 01:39:11,850
